-- title:
--   Pythagorean splitting of a vector along a unit axis and across it
-- statement:
--   Let $E$ be a real inner product space, let $v \in E$ be a unit vector, $\|v\| = 1$, and let $p \in E$ be arbitrary. Write
--   $$\mathrm{across}(v,p) \;=\; p - \langle v, p\rangle\, v$$
--   for the component of $p$ orthogonal to $v$ (the "across-axis" part), so that $p = \langle v,p\rangle v + \mathrm{across}(v,p)$. Then
--   $$\|p\|^2 \;=\; \langle v, p\rangle^2 \;+\; \|\mathrm{across}(v,p)\|^2 .$$
--   Here $\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle$ is the real inner product of $E$.
--
--   This is the Pythagorean identity underlying every cone computation: a point is described by its coordinate $a = \langle v,p\rangle$ along the axis and the length $b = \|\mathrm{across}(v,p)\|$ of its transverse part, and the identity $\|p\|^2 = a^2 + b^2$ is what converts angular conditions on $p$ into algebraic relations between $a$, $b$ and $\|p\|$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/dbenbenn/quadratic-forms-sobolev/blob/7a1a680db2124d46ce370c91fd450aa454edf491/QuadraticFormsSobolev/ConeGap.lean#L34-L42

